MID_EV14_050_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_050_m01_001: Father! Father! So this is where you were.
MID_EV14_050_m01_002: You're talking to Mother at her grave again.
MID_EV14_050_m01_003: Yes. I was just telling Hilaria that you're leaving to\ntrain at Kalla's temple next week.
MID_EV14_050_m01_004: You'll take care of yourself when I'm gone, right?
MID_EV14_050_m01_005: You work so hard. What's going to happen when no\none's here to make you stop?
MID_EV14_050_m01_006: I might have Buccar grab you every day and sit you\ndown for a nap!
MID_EV14_050_m01_007: Ahaha. I'll be damned. When was it that you started\nparenting me?
MID_EV14_050_m01_008: Really, Father. Is there something I can do?
MID_EV14_050_m01_009: After I get back from the temple, I want to take\ncare of you.
MID_EV14_050_m01_010: Something you can do? Let me think... Alright,\nvery well! Here's what you can do.
MID_EV14_050_m01_011: Live a long life, Leilidahna, and see as much of this\nworld as you can.
MID_EV14_050_m01_012: Learn different opinions, feel your feelings fully,\nand come home to tell me about all of it.
MID_EV14_050_m01_013: And what's most important—be happy, always.
MID_EV14_050_m01_014: I know, novel! A father wanting his daughter's\nhappiness. But I wish for that above all else.
MID_EV14_050_m01_015: Do you hear me, Leilidahna? I want you to always\nremember...
MID_EV14_050_m01_016: Leda. LEDA! Kalla wants to see you!
MID_EV14_050_m01_017: <NCA>Awaken.
MID_EV14_050_m01_018: Aaaah...
MID_EV14_050_m01_019: You're crying. Did you have a bad dream?
MID_EV14_050_m01_020: No, no—not a dream.
MID_EV14_050_m01_021: A reminder of the times I can't get back to.
MID_EV14_050_m01_022: Do you mean...your dad?
MID_EV14_050_m01_023: Mu, as a friend who's always stuck by my side,\ntell me honestly.
MID_EV14_050_m01_024: What would you do if I died? Would you go back to\nthe country?
MID_EV14_050_m01_025: I don't like this question. Is it supposed to be a joke?\nIt's not very funny...
MID_EV14_050_m01_026: It's just a question. I don't have a death wish.
MID_EV14_050_m01_027: OK. Well, I hope not.
MID_EV14_050_m01_028: Let me ask it this way. What will you do when I've\naccomplished my goal?
MID_EV14_050_m01_029: I dunno. I hadn't really thought about it.
MID_EV14_050_m01_030: Go back to my aunt's house, I guess? But there's\nsomething I have to do first.
MID_EV14_050_m01_031: I gotta find my dad.
MID_EV14_050_m01_032: <NCA>Ask about Mu's father.
MID_EV14_050_m01_033: What was your father like? You haven't said much\nabout him.
MID_EV14_050_m01_034: That's because my mom kicked him out when I\nwas little.
MID_EV14_050_m01_035: Oh...I see. What did he do to get himself kicked out?
MID_EV14_050_m01_036: I was really young, so I don't know what happened\nbetween the two of them.
MID_EV14_050_m01_037: But my dad was always nice to me... He didn't give\nme any reason to not like him.
MID_EV14_050_m01_038: So I want to find him, wherever he is, and talk to\nthe guy again.
MID_EV14_050_m01_039: I think that's a good idea—seeing your father while\nyou still can.
MID_EV14_050_m01_040: Whatever you have to say to him, say it when you\nhave the chance.
MID_EV14_051_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_051_m01_001: Leilidahna! There you are. The details of your next\nmatch have been finalized.
MID_EV14_051_m01_002: Uhh... Why is this coming from you? Where's Anna?
MID_EV14_051_m01_003: Otherwise occupied—as she often is these days.\nWaylaid by a request from my brother.
MID_EV14_051_m01_004: I've been asked to share this message in her stead.
MID_EV14_051_m01_005: Running the games has got to be a busy job. Who\nknows what she's up to.
MID_EV14_051_m01_006: <NCA>Ask about the match.
MID_EV14_051_m01_007: So, who's our next opponent?
MID_EV14_051_m01_008: You may already be familiar with her—it's Theodora,\nqueen of Saramis.
MID_EV14_051_m01_009: You should know too... Bertrand is advancing to the\nnext round.
MID_EV14_051_m01_010: Should both of you win your next matches, you will\nface each other in the finals.
MID_EV14_051_m01_011: One more victory, then I kill Bertrand.
MID_EV14_051_m01_012: Leilidahna, may I ask...what will you do after you\ntake your revenge?
MID_EV14_051_m01_013: I...can't really think about the future right now.
MID_EV14_051_m01_014: But—I'd move on to another target. More of the\nvillains behind the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_051_m01_015: You know how much affection I have for you,\nas my blood.
MID_EV14_051_m01_016: Sometimes, when I look at you, I can't help but be\nreminded of Cohen.
MID_EV14_051_m01_017: I would like to help you however I can.
MID_EV14_051_m01_018: I appreciate the thought, but this is my fight.
MID_EV14_051_m01_019: But...do you know about the Supreme Arcs?
MID_EV14_051_m01_020: I've heard of Arcs before. Weapons of unusual power\nthat the temples control.
MID_EV14_051_m01_021: Yes. And as you'd expect, the Supreme Arcs are\nforemost among them.
MID_EV14_051_m01_022: They are weapons of exceptional power prepared\nespecially for the gods.
MID_EV14_051_m01_023: Does that mean you have one of them too?
MID_EV14_051_m01_024: I do. It is known as Kalla's Bow.
MID_EV14_051_m01_025: Because of its power, it has been hidden beneath my\nmain temple in Caelus county.
MID_EV14_051_m01_026: Proceed there, and recover my bow from\nthe temple...
MID_EV14_051_m01_027: and at that time, I will lend you the bow.
MID_EV14_051_m01_028: I appreciate the offer, but...why would I be allowed\nto have this?
MID_EV14_051_m01_029: It's true that the Supreme Arcs must be kept under\nthe control of the gods.
MID_EV14_051_m01_030: But we are permitted to lend them to those who have\npassed a test.
MID_EV14_051_m01_031: If you are so inclined, I would suggest making for the\ntemple and undertaking the test.
MID_EV14_051_m01_032: I appreciate your generosity, Kalla.
MID_EV14_052_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_052_m01_001: The months since the qualifiers seem to have taken\na toll on you.
MID_EV14_052_m01_002: Checking on your opponent's health before a match?\nActing a little overconfident, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV14_052_m01_003: <NCA>Observe Theodora.
MID_EV14_052_m01_004: For your part...you seem to be doing better \nthan you were in the qualifiers.
MID_EV14_052_m01_005: Much more composed, certainly, than you were in\nthe match against Alexandra.
MID_EV14_052_m01_006: But I still don't like your chances. I have to win,\nand I'm going to.
MID_EV14_052_m01_007: I did not think words would sway you. But I must\nwarn you, my stance is equally firm.
MID_EV14_052_m01_008: For I carry the long-held dream of a million\nSaraminians upon my back.
MID_EV14_052_m01_009: This is a fight, not a head count. You don't win\nbecause you have more people on your shoulders.
MID_EV14_052_m01_010: So you say. We shall test that claim in battle.
MID_EV14_052_m01_011: While we are here, indulge me in this. What would\nyou ask for at the end of the games?
MID_EV14_052_m01_012: <NCA>Tell her your wish.
MID_EV14_052_m01_013: <NCB>Ask to start the match.
MID_EV14_052_m01_014: <ACA>My wish is to kill the man Dagsion calls the\nWhite-Maned Demon. Bertrand.
MID_EV14_052_m01_015: <ACA>After I beat you here, I'll face him in the next match.\nThen my wish is as good as granted.
MID_EV14_052_m01_016: <ACA>So it is revenge you desire.
MID_EV14_052_m01_017: <ACA>I am surprised to hear of your history with him.\nYour wish puts me in a difficult position.
MID_EV14_052_m01_018: <ACA>I have plans of my own for the White-Maned Demon,\nso I cannot allow you to kill him.
MID_EV14_052_m01_019: <ACA>And I can't allow you to recruit him. I have to do\nit soon—there's not much time left.
MID_EV14_052_m01_020: <ACB>What does it matter? Let's hurry up and get this\nover with.
MID_EV14_052_m01_021: <ACB>I...don't have much time left. The sooner we\nsettle this, the better.
MID_EV14_052_m01_022: Why such haste, if I may ask?
MID_EV14_052_m01_023: Is it possible that you have begun to hear the voice\nas well?
MID_EV14_052_m01_024: You mean— I thought as much.
MID_EV14_052_m01_025: I know the vihuela you carry is no ordinary\ninstrument.
MID_EV14_052_m01_026: Unless I miss my guess, it is one of Drake's treasures,\nlike my right arm.
MID_EV14_052_m01_027: I know that this will sound hollow coming from me,\nbut I advise getting rid of it.
MID_EV14_052_m01_028: I can't. Obsidian is a house heirloom.
MID_EV14_052_m01_029: Besides...I hear the voice all the time, even when I'm\nnot playing—even now.
MID_EV14_052_m01_030: Right this moment, it's echoing from the depths of\nthe earth, telling me to kill you. To tear you apart.
MID_EV14_052_m01_031: I am impressed you are this far gone and still in\ncontrol of your faculties.
MID_EV14_052_m01_032: Perhaps something in you is unlike all the others who\nwere corrupted by Drake's treasures.
MID_EV14_052_m01_033: Then again, it may be mercy on my part to end your\nvendetta here.
MID_EV14_052_m01_034: Let us begin, Leda, that we might see whose\nwill prevails.
MID_EV14_052_m01_035: Yes, let's put this behind us. Prepare to lose,\nYour Majesty.
MID_EV14_053_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_053_m01_001: I never expected to lose. It is no small thing for your\ntenacity to exceed mine.
MID_EV14_053_m01_002: We both know I won by the thinnest of margins.\nLuck was on my side, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV14_053_m01_003: You can act a little prouder to have defeated the\nmighty Queen Theodora, if only for my sake.
MID_EV14_053_m01_004: <NCA>Thank her.
MID_EV14_053_m01_005: <ACA>Thank you. I'll take the compliment.
MID_EV14_053_m01_006: Forgive me if I speak out of turn here.
MID_EV14_053_m01_007: But you must be aware by now that it is wise to be\ncareful with that vihuela.
MID_EV14_053_m01_008: It promises incredible strength, but in return it will\neat away at your soul.
MID_EV14_053_m01_009: Arranging this for you may prove challenging, but...
MID_EV14_053_m01_010: I do know someone who can make a ward that will\nsuppress these thoughts.
MID_EV14_053_m01_011: It was not so long ago that I helped her craft one\nfor myself.
MID_EV14_053_m01_012: If you wish, I can inquire into having one made\nfor you as well.
MID_EV14_053_m01_013: I appreciate the offer, but that won't be necessary.
MID_EV14_053_m01_014: Soon, my wish will be granted. I just have to hold\non a little longer.
MID_EV14_053_m01_015: Living long enough to slit Bertrand's throat...\nThat's enough for me.
MID_EV14_053_m01_016: Besides, with Obsidian's voice comes its strength.
MID_EV14_053_m01_017: If there is power to be gained by giving myself,\nbody and soul, to darkness...
MID_EV14_053_m01_018: then I have no choice but to do so.
MID_EV14_053_m01_019: I understand your feelings toward it. Mine were\nmuch the same.
MID_EV14_053_m01_020: They— They were?
MID_EV14_053_m01_021: I knew that this arm would one day exact its toll.
MID_EV14_053_m01_022: Yet I had no choice but to accept its power and\naccomplish what I could with the time afforded me.
MID_EV14_053_m01_023: We have more in common than I thought.
MID_EV14_053_m01_024: Heh. Indeed we do.
MID_EV14_053_m01_025: I shall take my leave of you now. May fortune favor\nyou in the arena.